-- Performance pass (docs/plans/perf-pass.md). Departures and the Today board read the newest 300 open job_posts, ordered by coalesce(posted_at, first_seen_at) descending, out of up to 10,000 open posts; without an index on that expression every request reads and sorts every open post. This partial index holds the open posts only, by that expression, so the read walks it backwards and stops after 300 (the tie on id is sorted within equal times). No table or column changes and no unique index, so nothing old code writes can be refused. Expand only: one index on an existing table.
CREATE INDEX "job_posts_open_newest" ON "job_posts" USING btree (coalesce("job_posts"."posted_at", "job_posts"."first_seen_at")) WHERE "job_posts"."closed_at" is null;
